infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title Waterfall latency: each tree level adds a round trip
  desc Children fetch on mount, so independent requests serialize down the tree — until you hoist them
  order asc
  sequences
    - label Fetch user · 0–200 ms
      desc ProfilePage mounts and requests the user — the first 200 ms round trip.
    - label Fetch posts · 200–400 ms
      desc Posts mounts only after the user commits, so its request starts one round trip late.
    - label Fetch comments · 400–600 ms
      desc Comments mounts only after posts commit — three serial hops, 600 ms before any server time.
    - label Hoist + Promise.all · ~200 ms
      desc Issue the independent requests together from the top component — one round trip, ~3× faster.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #6366f1 #10b981
